# SLP Dealer Guard: every deploy is verified by comparing the server-side
# md5sum to the local working tree, so these files must round-trip
# byte-identically regardless of how core.autocrlf happens to be set on the
# machine doing the commit. They are stored in git with literal CRLF, and
# -text disables end-of-line conversion on both check-in and checkout.
#
# Upstream SLP plugins are never edited. Two of them are PINNED, and that is
# a different rule: release-pins.csv and Publish's $Upstream table carry md5s
# for store-locator-le/js/slp_core.js and slp_core.min.js, because
# slp_avalon.js cites lines 1720, 1808 and 1842 of that file by number and an
# SLP auto-update moving them is what the pins exist to catch. Both files are
# stored LF; without the rule below a fresh clone under core.autocrlf=true
# checks them out CRLF and both pins fail before Verify starts. Issue 34.
# Stopping git converting a file is not editing that file.
slp_avalon/** -text
store-locator-le/js/** -text
#
# The build, test and publish tooling is verified by md5 the same way, and
# release-pins.csv pins .gitattributes itself. Without these four lines a
# fresh clone under core.autocrlf=true checks all of them out as CRLF and
# every hash in Publish-Step14's tables is wrong before it starts.
build/** -text
test/** -text
*.ps1 -text
.gitattributes -text
